Ship 360 rather than 384 as the default height of the WEBTV codec profiles:
16:9 does not divide into 384 (1280x720 to h=384 wants 682.67, so every path
rounds it its own way), while 360 is a whole 640 for 16:9 and 480 for 4:3.

Ours, on top of patch 100 (tvheadend#2117).  Only affects a fresh install.

--- data/conf/transcoder/codecs.orig
+++ data/conf/transcoder/codecs
@@ -3,7 +3,7 @@
         "description": "WEBTV codec VP8",
         "name": "webtv-vp8",
         "codec_name": "libvpx",
-        "height": 384,
+        "height": 360,
         "deadline": 1,
         "crf": 28,
         "cpu-used": 8
@@ -12,7 +12,7 @@
         "description": "WEBTV codec VP8 VAAPI",
         "name": "webtv-vp8-vaapi",
         "codec_name": "vp8_vaapi",
-        "height": 384,
+        "height": 360,
         "bit_rate": 1500,
         "max_bit_rate": 2000,
         "hwaccel": true,
@@ -22,7 +22,7 @@
         "description": "WEBTV codec VP9",
         "name": "webtv-vp9",
         "codec_name": "libvpx-vp9",
-        "height": 384,
